# [type] with no body declares a phantom type — a type with no constructors.
# The empty-body form parses as a structural alias with an empty dict body,
# producing Value::Dict{ entries: {} } at runtime — an empty constructor dict.
# In DisplayVisitor format: Dict({})
#
# [@PhantomT 42] is a TypeAssert. During bootstrap, all TypeAssert checks pass
# because the unknown sentinel is consistent with every type.
[PhantomT: [type]
 val:       [@PhantomT 42]]
=== out
Dict({"PhantomT": Dict({}), "val": Int(42)})
